From: IrfanMohammad <irfan@graphiant.com>
Date: Thu, 28 Sep 2023 17:39:57 +0000
Subject: - Optimize xpath filtering for oper get subscr

 1. When the requested xpath is "/*" or "/module-name:*", we can
    short-circuit the check if the subscr is relevant.

 2. sysrepo-monitoring module oper may not need to check
    `sr_modinfo_module_data_oper_required` as often as it does.
    Most of the time, it is required.

 3. When a single module is queried for sysrepo-monitoring, don't
    process all modules.

 4. Don't acquire locks for modules without subscriptions for
    sysrepo-monitoring

- API to check sr_module_has_change_sub efficiently

Currently, the only way to check if a module has a subscription is via
sysrepo-monitoring and that is extremely inefficient.

When applications poll for a subscription to be created, it is better to
have a simple api to first check whether the module has any
subscriptions.
